> I'm fitting a latent growth curve model as can be seen below. However,
> as I add additional terms, my CFI, TLI, & SRMR shows *worse* fit.

I get (0.5-11):

 > fitMeasures(linear, c("chisq", "df", "cfi", "tli", "srmr", "rmsea"))
    chisq       df      cfi      tli     srmr    rmsea
3892.827   50.000    0.862    0.876    0.015    0.395

 > fitMeasures(quadratic, c("chisq", "df", "cfi", "tli", "srmr", "rmsea"))
    chisq       df      cfi      tli     srmr    rmsea
2258.283   46.000    0.920    0.922    0.007    0.313

 > fitMeasures(cubic, c("chisq", "df", "cfi", "tli", "srmr", "rmsea"))
    chisq       df      cfi      tli     srmr    rmsea
1782.124   41.000    0.937    0.931    0.010    0.294

All fit measures improve, except the srmr in the cubic case. The latter
model, however, produced some negative variances.

Yves.

